{# UX funnel §4 (issue #147), restyled in docs/features/auth-ux-redesign.md
   §4.1: the error and the rescue in one alert under the heading, after any
   failed password sign-in. Identical for a wrong password and an unknown
   address - it must never hint whether the address has an account. The
   rescue is a plain link: the address follows via sessionStorage, the typed
   password stays on the login endpoint.
   Parameters: throttled (bool), return_params. #}
<div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert">
    <p class="fw-medium mb-1">
        {{ (throttled ? 'auth.failure_helper.throttled' : 'auth.failure_helper.title')|trans }}
    </p>

    {% if not throttled %}
        <p class="mb-2">{{ 'auth.failure_helper.vault_tip'|trans }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    <a class="btn btn-outline-danger mt-1" href="{{ path('sign_in_link_request', return_params) }}">
        <i class="bi bi-envelope me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ 'auth.failure_helper.link'|trans }}
    </a>
</div>
